a6d6e635e9ac3f54e3e3df0a35a5ae2a79039a32cf01924ed4fee71b","file":"preprints/Sharp-integral-fillings-in-CAT(0)-spaces-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":26,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"4182991eb12e92878c66681d99ba1163c5b976285c0c2652214f078ceaaeb726","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Sharp-integral-fillings-in-CAT(0)-spaces-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:2d1cf82fa6d6e635e9ac3f54e3e3df0a35a5ae2a79039a32cf01924ed4fee71b","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Sharp-integral-fillings-in-CAT%280%29-spaces-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L26"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $X$ be a proper CAT(0) space and $n\\ge2$ an integer.\nEvery compactly supported $T\\in\\I_n(X)$ with $\\partial T=0$ admits a\ncompactly supported $S\\in\\I_{n+1}(X)$ such that\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main}\n \\partial S=T,\\qquad\n \\M(S)\\le c_n\\M(T)^{(n+1)/n}\n =\\frac{\\M(T)^{(n+1)/n}}\n {(n+1)^{(n+1)/n}\\omega_{n+1}^{1/n}}.\n\\end{equation}\nThere is no restriction on the dimension of $X$ or on the integer\nmultiplicities of the currents. The coefficient is optimal."}
